                <pb facs="1446" n="1426" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1426"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>President Truman and Prime Minister Attlee held their third and fourth meetings
                    on December 6 from 11:40 a. m. to 12:30 p. m. and from 3:30 p. m. to 4:35 p. m.
                    The discussions dealt with economic problems, Western Europe, and accelerated
                    defense efforts. There was no discussion of Korea and the Far East. The minutes
                    of the meetings are scheduled for publication in volume III.</p>
                <p>Also on December 6, Prime Minister Attlee gave an address before the National
                    Press Club, the salient portions of which are printed in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Keesing’s Contemporary Archives, 1950–1952</hi>, page 11, 334.</p>
            </div>
